# The staging build: `vite build --mode staging --outDir dist-staging`.
#
# Since the gateway cutover the website calls only same-origin /api/** and the
# gateway (prooflab-staging-web-bff) holds the backend addresses. The six
# VITE_*_URL lines below are NOT read by the website any more and are not in
# the build; they stay as the written record of which staging services exist
# (src/lib/apiRouteContract.test.ts fails if the site starts reading one).
# What the build does take from this file: VITE_PUBLIC_BUCKET and
# VITE_ASYNC_TRANSCRIPTION. The bucket name is also how the production release
# guard recognises a staging build, so keep it a prooflab-staging-* name.
#
# Plain `npm run dev -- --mode staging` can no longer sign in: the dev server
# has no /api route and answers with the app page. For a local run use the
# gateway harness instead:
#   npx vite --mode staging --config scripts/dev-tools/harness/vite.local-bff.config.ts --port 5199 --strictPort
# (with scripts/dev-tools/harness/bff_local_stack.ts running).
#
# None of these are secrets: the API key is a public browser key, the same one
# as in .env.production, and every URL is a public Cloud Run address gated by
# the app's own auth, not by URL secrecy.
#
# VITE_ASYNC_TRANSCRIPTION gates the queued-transcription UI added in Step 6D
# (VoiceExplainModal.tsx). It must stay unset in .env.production until a
# separate, approved production rollout - see that file's own comment.
VITE_BACKEND=google
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIzaSyCNv0YWVP5QTDRb4WPVccmosCMC8cH7nnw
VITE_AUTH_BRIDGE_URL=https://prooflab-staging-auth-bridge-ysn2mpe6sa-el.a.run.app
VITE_POSTGREST_URL=https://prooflab-staging-api-ysn2mpe6sa-el.a.run.app
VITE_FILES_URL=https://prooflab-staging-files-ysn2mpe6sa-el.a.run.app
VITE_FUNCTIONS_URL=https://prooflab-staging-functions-ysn2mpe6sa-el.a.run.app
VITE_PUBLIC_BUCKET=prooflab-staging-public-508214
VITE_TRANSCRIBER_URL=https://prooflab-staging-transcriber-ysn2mpe6sa-el.a.run.app
VITE_ACCOUNTS_URL=https://prooflab-staging-accounts-ysn2mpe6sa-el.a.run.app
VITE_ASYNC_TRANSCRIPTION=true
